# Writer 11 (tally 2.1, 2.1-9). L §5.10: "bal(x, d start) of q ... read[s] the same points as [its total does]": on
# 02-01, the start of the day is before wage, and the end after it.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind couples: parties
kind savings: place PLN min 0
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if k.owner == ania_tomek then 0 else 1
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
place acc: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input wage_day: date
input wage_amt: money PLN
input out_day: date
input out_amt: money PLN
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule community = if p == ania_tomek then 1 else 0
move wage: transfers
  on wage_day
  leg cash from world to konto amount wage_amt
move out: transfers
  on out_day
  leg cash from konto to acc amount out_amt
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-02-01 start) of ania_tomek, bal(konto, 2026-02-01) of ania_tomek, bal(konto, 2026-02-02 start) of ania_tomek

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  couples + [ania_tomek] lives 2010-06-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  opening[acc] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
  wage_day = 2026-02-01
  wage_amt = 100.00 PLN
  out_day = 2026-03-01
  out_amt = 30.00 PLN
=== expect
q: (0.00 PLN, 100.00 PLN, 100.00 PLN)
  cut 2026-01-01
